       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. 20 mg once daily is double the FDA-labeled maximum for amlodipine in adults, which is 10 mg once daily. Doses above 10 mg raise the risk of peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia, and they usually add little blood pressure benefit.\n\nYou could do one of these instead:\n1. **Enter 10 mg PO once daily**, the maximum standard dose. This is the usual choice if you want the most from amlodipine.\n2. **Start at 5 mg PO once daily** and titrate up. This is typical for a new start.\n3. **Add a second agent**, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide, if 10 mg isn't controlling the blood pressure. I can enter that order too.\n\nIf you really do want 20 mg, for example because of a specialist recommendation or a documented plan, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. Which would you like?"
      }
     ],
